From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:01:27 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Testing guide: a long suite takes --basetemp on a real
 disk

pytest's default base directory under the system temporary directory kept
thousands of tmp_path directories across sweeps on a server whose /tmp is a
fixed-inode tmpfs.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
---
 docs/developer/TESTING-RELIABILITY-SYSTEM.md | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/developer/TESTING-RELIABILITY-SYSTEM.md b/docs/developer/TESTING-RELIABILITY-SYSTEM.md
index a6d6f5ee..ebbf5c98 100644
--- a/docs/developer/TESTING-RELIABILITY-SYSTEM.md
+++ b/docs/developer/TESTING-RELIABILITY-SYSTEM.md
@@ -244,6 +244,14 @@ pytest
 pytest -m "not tier_c"
 ```
 
+For a long suite, or repeated sweeps, give pytest a base temporary directory
+on a real disk: `pytest tests --basetemp=$HOME/scratch/pytest-tmp -m ...`.
+By default pytest keeps the `tmp_path` directories of its last three runs
+under the system temporary directory. On a server where `/tmp` is a tmpfs
+with a fixed number of inodes, thousands of them, together with any other
+leftovers, can fill it and stop every session on the machine. `--basetemp`
+is emptied at the start of each run, so give each concurrent run its own.
+
